    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald O'Donovan are delighted to bring to the market 3 Ballycar Road, Newmarket-on-Fergus, an exceptional three-bedroom semi-detached home which has been beautifully maintained and upgraded by its current owners. \n\nPresented in excellent turnkey condition throughout, this impressive property offers well-proportioned accommodation with a high standard of finish. The property is flooded with natural light throughout, creating a bright, warm and welcoming atmosphere.\n\nThe ground floor accommodation comprises an inviting sitting room, a downstairs WC and a superb extended kitchen and dining area. The kitchen has been extended to create a bright and spacious open-plan kitchen and dining area, providing an excellent space for both everyday family living and entertaining.\n\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms along with the main family bathroom. The property also benefits from a fully converted attic space, currently providing excellent additional storage.\n\nOutside, the property is complemented by a lovely garden which has been exceptionally well maintained and is presented in immaculate condition. The garden provides a pleasant outdoor space and is a credit to the current owners.\n\nLocated in the heart of Newmarket-on-Fergus, the property is ideally positioned within easy reach of a wide range of local amenities including shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, sporting facilities and public transport links. The village also provides convenient access to Shannon, Ennis and Limerick, while Shannon Airport is just a short drive away.\n\n3 Ballycar Road is a superb family home which combines excellent accommodation, a high standard of presentation and a fantastic location. The turnkey condition, extended kitchen and dining area, bright interiors and additional attic storage make this a particularly attractive home and early viewing is highly recommended without delay."
      },
